# 1. C Program Compilation Process

The C program does not directly become an executable file.

It passes through **four stages**:

```text
Source Code (.c)
       ↓
Preprocessor
       ↓
Preprocessed Code (.i)
       ↓
Compiler
       ↓
Assembly Code (.s)
       ↓
Assembler
       ↓
Object Code (.o)
       ↓
Linker
       ↓
Executable File
       ↓
Execution
```

---

# 2. Step 1 — Preprocessor

## **Description**

The **preprocessor** is the first stage of the C compilation process.

It processes all preprocessor directives before the actual compilation starts.

Common preprocessor directives are:

```c
#include
#define
#ifdef
#ifndef
#if
#else
#endif
```

## **Example**

```c
#include <stdio.h>

#define MESSAGE "Hello World"

int main()
{
    printf("%s\n", MESSAGE);

    return 0;
}
```

## **Command**

```bash
gcc -E program.c -o program.i
```

## **Output**

```text
program.i
```

The `.i` file contains the **preprocessed source code**.

## **Flow**

```text
program.c
    ↓
Preprocessor
    ↓
program.i
```

---

# 3. Step 2 — Compiler

## **Description**

The **compiler** converts the preprocessed C source code into **assembly language**.

It also checks the program for syntax and language-related errors.

## **Command**

```bash
gcc -S program.i -o program.s
```

## **Output**

```text
program.s
```

The `.s` file contains **assembly language instructions**.

## **Flow**

```text
program.i
    ↓
Compiler
    ↓
program.s
```

---

# 4. Step 3 — Assembler

## **Description**

The **assembler** converts the assembly language code into **object code**.

The object file contains machine-level code that can later be linked.

## **Command**

```bash
gcc -c program.s -o program.o
```

## **Output**

```text
program.o
```

## **Flow**

```text
program.s
    ↓
Assembler
    ↓
program.o
```

---

# 5. Step 4 — Linker

## **Description**

The **linker** combines the object file with required libraries and resolves external references.

For example:

```c
printf()
```

is provided by the C standard library.

## **Command**

```bash
gcc program.o -o program
```

## **Output**

```text
program
```

## **Flow**

```text
program.o + Libraries
          ↓
        Linker
          ↓
      Executable
```

---

# 6. Execution

After the executable file is created, it can be executed using:

```bash
./program
```

### **Output**

```text
Hello World
```

