# 7. Complete Example

## **Step 1 — Create the C File**

```bash
vi program.c
```

## **Step 2 — Write the Program**

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    printf("Hello World\n");

    return 0;
}
```

## **Step 3 — Save the File**

In `vi`:

```text
Esc
:wq
```

## **Step 4 — Preprocessing**

```bash
gcc -E program.c -o program.i
```

Creates:

```text
program.i
```

## **Step 5 — Compilation**

```bash
gcc -S program.i -o program.s
```

Creates:

```text
program.s
```

## **Step 6 — Assembly**

```bash
gcc -c program.s -o program.o
```

Creates:

```text
program.o
```

## **Step 7 — Linking**

```bash
gcc program.o -o program
```

Creates:

```text
program
```

## **Step 8 — Execution**

```bash
./program
```

Output:

```text
Hello World
```

