# 8. One Command Compilation

GCC can perform all the required compilation stages automatically.

```bash
gcc program.c -o program
```

Then execute:

```bash
./program
```

If the output file name is not specified:

```bash
gcc program.c
```

GCC normally creates:

```text
a.out
```

Execute it using:

```bash
./a.out
```

